 players stumble across a dangerous fellow and kill him. Now they've committed a crime and potentially breached some issue of their splat's Masquerade, leading to further storytelling based on that.<br /> <br /> Another thing in Dungeons and Dragons, and especially in the modules, is that the progression shows itself in scaling challenge ratings. First you kill some rats, then some goblins, then a hobgoblin, then a hobgoblin leading a bunch of goblins, then an ogre, all manner of increasing difficulty. And your characters can generally deal with it, because everyone's class is built around combat in one way or another, and the levels they've gained confronting previous challenges have made them more capable of dealing with future ones.<br /> <br /> But in World of Darkness, if the players finish their chapter based around the haunted house, one may decide to buy a skill point in Brawl to represent his newfound confidence with hand-to-hand combat after dealing with that guy, while another might purchase a point in Occult to show that their character has finally graduated from occult-hobbyist to full-fledged explorer, and another might gain some Streetwise, since they had to deal with a gang when it came to hiding the evidence of their activity. Either way, if the next encounter is a combat-oriented one, the only character who's gained any advantage in that situation is the one who raised a point in Brawl.<br /> <br /> Now depending on your interests regarding the editions of World of Darkness, I'd suggest checking out something like Darkening Sky for classic World of Darkness. It's a series of pre-made adventures for five of the classic splats, Mage, Vampire, Werewolf, Changeling and Inquisitor, set during an eclipse during the Dark Ages. They show, sort of, how stories might go. They do tend to be more linear than some peoples games, but that's the price of a pre-made. In new World of Darkness, Mummy just came out with the Avarice Chronicle, which is sort of the same thing but a longer adventure and confined to Mummy. Obviously you know about the Storytelling Adventure System books, but these are a couple newer ones. There's a longer chronicle in the back of all the Hunter books. And for examples of other people's stories you might look for actual plays from the World of Darkness. I believe there's a thread of them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/130083-any-blogs-or-notes-on-existing-former-vampire-chronicles\">here</a>. RPG.net seems to have more than our forums but there's more than a few here. And if you're looking for a group I do believe we have a play-by-post subforum somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-18-2015, 10:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T06:24:04-07:00","id":632191,"title":"","content":"MODERATOR OR ADMIN PLEASE DELETE MY ACCOUNT AS I WILL NOT BE RETURNING TO THIS FORUM EVER AGAIN.<br /> <br /> I removed all of my posts because I felt attacked on this website, disrespected, treated unfairly, and otherwise felt nothing but hostility from the members here. Good bye.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1707,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1707-baldurkhan","user":"Baldurkhan","date":". 08-20-2015, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1707-baldurkhan","name":"Baldurkhan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"De