 adding lightsabers and starships to nWoD. It can be done mechanically, but why would you? It's a completely different tone and feel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T17:54:01-07:00","id":632888,"title":"","content":"MODERATOR OR ADMIN PLEASE DELETE MY ACCOUNT AS I WILL NOT BE RETURNING TO THIS FORUM EVER AGAIN.<br /> <br /> I removed all of my posts because I felt attacked on this website, disrespected, treated unfairly, and otherwise felt nothing but hostility from the members here. Good bye.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1707,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1707-baldurkhan","user":"Baldurkhan","date":". 08-20-2015, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1707-baldurkhan","name":"Baldurkhan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T18:49:28-07:00","id":632946,"title":"","content":"MODERATOR OR ADMIN PLEASE DELETE MY ACCOUNT AS I WILL NOT BE RETURNING TO THIS FORUM EVER AGAIN.<br /> <br /> I removed all of my posts because I felt attacked on this website, disrespected, treated unfairly, and otherwise felt nothing but hostility from the members here. Good bye.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1707,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1707-baldurkhan","user":"Baldurkhan","date":". 08-20-2015, 05:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1707-baldurkhan","name":"Baldurkhan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T07:52:17-07:00","id":633476,"title":"","content":"I think it's a cool project. Do you really need another reason beyond &quot;I want to play/GM this D&amp;D module, and I like the Storytelling Sustem better than the D20 system?&quot;<br /> <br /> I've been toying with an idea like this on and off myself for a long time now. My reason why is that I like the setting(s) of D&amp;D, but I want to play a dramatic story telling game in the setting, rather than a wargame. I would like to see a take on D&amp;D where the adventuring life takes a psychological toll on the adventurers. Where combat is a last resort, not the default expectation. I want to deconstruct the pulp fantasy/adventure worlds of D&amp;D by running them with a system geared towards personal horror and drama.<br /> <br /> And beside that, I love the idea of D&amp;D's alignment system, but hate the way D&amp;D handles it, and I think a dual morality/integrity system with one track for moral/amoral and one track for lawful/chaotic and Breaking Points in both directions for each would capture the concept infinitely better than the 9 boxes do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T14:04:45-07:00","id":633772,"title"